        "original_id": "72bc5851-0965-5c9d-9f1b-7656c2afb985",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Graham Hill, Richie Ginther, Bruce McLaren\n- Events: 1962 Italian Grand Prix, 1963 Lombank Trophy\n- Teams/Organizations: Cooper, BRM\n- Products: BRM P57\n- Roles: racing driver, team owner, Formula One World Champion\n\nFacts:\n- Graham Hill was born on 15 February 1929 and died on 29 November 1975.\n- Graham Hill was a British racing driver and team owner from England.\n- Graham Hill won the Formula One World Championship twice.\n- At the 1962 Italian Grand Prix, Richie Ginther finished second.\n- At the 1962 Italian Grand Prix, Cooper driver Bruce McLaren finished third.\n- The 1963 Lombank Trophy was run over 50 laps.\n- British driver Graham Hill won the 1963 Lombank Trophy in a BRM P57.",
